e covariances via gradients</article-title>											<source>J Mach Learn Res</source>											<volume>7</volume>											<fpage>519</fpage>											<lpage>549</lpage>										</element-citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0040028-b014"><element-citation publication-type="journal">											<person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mukherjee</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name></person-group>											<year>2006</year>											<article-title>Estimation of gradients and coordinate covariation in classification</article-title>											<source>J Mach Learn Res</source>											<volume>7</volume>											<fpage>2481</fpage>											<lpage>2514</lpage>										</element-citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0040028-b015"><element-citation publication-type="book">											<person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mukherjee</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>DX</given-names></name></person-group>											<year>2006</year>											<source>Gradient learning and feature selection on manifolds. Working paper 06&#x02013;20</source>											<publisher-loc>Durham (North Carolina)</publisher-loc>											<publisher-name>Department of Statistical Science, Duke University</publisher-name>											<comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://ftp.stat.duke.edu/WorkingPapers/06-20.html">http://ftp.stat.duke.edu/WorkingPapers/06&#x02013;20.html</ext-link>. Accessed 15 January 2008.</comment>										</element-citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0040028-b016"><element-citation publication-type="book">											<person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Guinney</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Maggioni</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><n